<title>USA: White House set on Tongass lumber supply - Murkowski.</title>
<headline>White House set on Tongass lumber supply - Murkowski.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alaskan U.S. Senator Frank Murkowski said Thursday the White House tentatively agreed to keep a transition supply of lumber flowing to two sawmills in southeast Alaska in an effort to break a stalemate over a national parks bill.</p>
<p>&quot;The current reality is that this is not a done deal,&quot; Murkowski, a Republican, said at a news conference.</p>
<p>But he had a draft of a letter initialed by White House Chief of Staff Leon Panetta to release lumber that was to go to the Ketchikan Pulp Mill to be available instead for two Ketchikan company sawmills.</p>
</text>
